Source texts and quotations
---------------------------

The texts under sources/buddha, sources/laozi, sources/confucius, sources/marcus-aurelius and
sources/epictetus are in the public domain worldwide or dedicated to the public domain under
CC0. The edition, translator, year and download location of each are recorded in
sources/PROVENANCE.md.

Quotations from Carl Gustav Jung are short excerpts from English editions published before
1931, which are in the public domain in the United States. Jung's work remains in copyright
in countries with a life-plus-70 term until 2032, so this repository contains excerpts only
and never a complete work.

Quotations from Charles T. Munger are brief excerpts from his public speeches and writings,
each cited to its source. No source text of his is included.

The quotations from Jung and Munger remain the property of their respective rights holders.
They are included as brief, cited excerpts for commentary and education, and they are not
covered by this repository's MIT licence.

